  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 141 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nHigh pressure will build into the Great Lakes region tonight into \nSaturday, providing subsidence and cooler northeasterly flow for \ncentral IL to provide for mostly clear skies and seasonably cool \ntemperatures. Lows tonight look to reach the mid 40s near and north \nof I-72 to around 50 south of I-70. Highs Saturday should be mainly \nin the lower 70s.\n\nA minor uptick in temperatures is expected for Sunday as a shortwave \npassing by to the north pushes a weak cold front toward IL Sunday, \ndisrupting the cool advection as winds turn southerly briefly. \nModels continue to keep all precipitation to the north of central IL \nwith this feature. Lows Saturday night look to be up a few degrees \nover most of the area with upper 40s to around 50. Highs Sunday look \nto be around the mid to upper 70s. \n\nAnother expansive surface high moves into the Great Lakes region \nMonday and Tuesday and exits toward the Mid-Atlantic coast midweek. \nThis will advect cooler air into central IL Monday and Tuesday for \nhighs mainly in the lower 70s, then south to southwest flow behind \nthe departing high will raise highs to near 80 for Wednesday through \nFriday. Under the influence of light winds and clear skies with the \nhigh pressure nearby, the coldest lows of the upcoming week are \nforecast for Monday night, with lower to mid 40s estimated at this \ntime. No precipitation is forecast through the end of next week.",
